================================================================================
Third-party design references
================================================================================

No third-party project's source code is vendored, copied, or redistributed
in this repository (see docs/legal-notices.md for how that was checked).
Two open-source Minecraft-compatible Rust projects are cited, by name and
by symbol, as engineering references in code comments and in docs/ — this
section records that fact and each project's license so a reader (or
counsel) does not have to reconstruct it from source-tree greps:

  * azalea (https://github.com/azalea-rs/azalea) — MIT license. Cited
    throughout crates/lodestone-ecs and docs/bevy-migration.md as a design
    reference for this workspace's own, independently written, ECS-based
    client architecture (schedule shape, resource ownership patterns).
    Not a dependency of this workspace; no azalea source is present here.

  * ferrumc (https://github.com/ferrumc-rs/ferrumc) — MIT license. Named
    in DESIGN.md among prior art surveyed while designing the protocol
    version seam. Not a dependency of this workspace; no ferrumc source
    is present here.

  * Pumpkin (https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin) — GPL-3.0 license, a
    copyleft license, unlike the two above. docs/plans/worldgen-rewrite.md
    records a detailed read of Pumpkin's source at a pinned commit and
    recommends adopting specific *engineering shapes* (a flattened density
    graph, thread-local buffer pools, a staged per-chunk dependency graph)
    for Lodestone's own, separately written, world-generation engine; it
    explicitly rejects using any of Pumpkin's placement/feature *behaviour*
    as an authority, in favour of this repository's own JVM oracles (see
    "Data sources" below). No Pumpkin source is vendored here, and none of
    the plan's named constructs (e.g. its `F64_BUFFER_POOL`, `FlatCache`,
    `StagedChunkEnum`) appear verbatim in this workspace's Rust source as
    of this NOTICE. Because Pumpkin is copyleft, its architectural
    influence on this repository — even absent literal copying — is the
    one third-party reference in this file that specifically warrants
    counsel's review before any of that plan is implemented.

================================================================================
Data sources
================================================================================

Behavioural parity with Minecraft is established by:

  * Mojang's own published data generators (packets.json, registries.json,
    blocks.json) and the game's real, unmodified server jar, run headless
    and read through its public API surface (never modified, never
    redistributed) by the oracle programs under */oracle-java/ and
    scripts/*-oracle/ in this repository (all Java source, all authored
    for this project — see docs/legal-notices.md).
  * A decompiled reference under .cache/, used for behaviour verification
    only, gitignored, and never committed to this repository.

No Mojang-authored source code, compiled class, or jar is checked into
this repository.
